    <briefdescription>
<para>Guarantees for retrieval and graph traversal consistency. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><bold>Determinism:</bold> SNAPSHOT_DETERMINISTIC <linebreak/>
 <bold>Isolation:</bold> All queries operate over a consistent snapshot at a single instant <linebreak/>
 <bold>Ordering:</bold> Graph traversal order is deterministic per snapshot</para>
<para>Queries return consistent snapshots captured at a single instant in time. Concurrent queries may see different snapshots (if model changes between queries), but each snapshot is internally consistent.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="invariant"><para>All edges and nodes in a query result are from the same snapshot instant </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="invariant"><para>Graph traversal (BFS, PPR) order is deterministic for a given snapshot </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="invariant"><para>Repeated queries with identical input yield identical results (same snapshot) </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="invariant"><para>Newer queries may see updates from model changes (different snapshot)</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para><bold>Non-deterministic aspect:</bold> Community detection algorithm is deterministic, but community ordering may vary across model versions (different graph structure). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
